WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:05.320
Luffy was inspired by Shanks to become a great
pirate, but what if that wasn’t the only

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:07.390
thing he learned from Shanks?

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:11.090
Because as we all know, Shanks is a LEGENDARY
swordsman.

00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:16.279
Or even better, what if Luffy had a completely
different mentor than Shanks to begin with,

00:00:16.279 --> 00:00:21.980
which leaves us with one of the most fascinating
questions in all of One Piece: what would

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:28.869
have happened, if instead of eating a devil
fruit, Luffy was trained to become a swordsman

00:00:28.869 --> 00:00:29.869
instead.

00:00:29.869 --> 00:00:33.430
And let’s kick this off where any good pirate
story begins, back in the bar.

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:38.430
And it is here that hungry child Luffy is
about to eat this devil fruit [ch 1, show

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:39.430
luffy about to eat the fruit].

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:44.260
But to really set up our what if scenario,
THIS TIME Shanks snatches the devil fruit

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:45.710
away.

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:49.930
Luffy is of course furious and demands to
have the fruit back, but Shanks and Lucky

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:51.399
Roux here [ch 1, show Lucky Roux holding up
the picture of a devil fruit] finally explain

00:00:51.399 --> 00:00:55.239
what a devil fruit is and why Luffy can’t
eat it.

00:00:55.239 --> 00:00:59.260
However, this isn’t enough for Luffy though
because, come on, what kid wouldn’t want

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:06.220
to eat a strange purple fruit, so he tries
to steal the devil fruit back multiple times.

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:09.610
So to finally stop Luffy, Shanks makes a deal.

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:15.600
If Luffy doesn’t try to eat the fruit, Shanks
will teach him how to use a sword.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:17.740
Oh boy, here we go.

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:19.590
This is about to get insane!

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:25.220
So of course, Luffy immediately agrees and
they get right into training.

00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:30.200
And wow, Luffy is going to need it because
at this point he is probably more likely to

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:33.810
cut off his own foot than he is to hit an
opponent.

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:38.829
But of course Shanks wouldn’t give him an
actual sword yet, so he’ll have a wooden

00:01:38.829 --> 00:01:42.640
practice sword for now and maybe a small dagger
or something.

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:48.320
That means for the next few years, Luffy will
be training with a sword, AND each time Shanks

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:53.020
comes back to the island Luffy is going to
be super excited to show off his new moves.

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:58.689
Now, to make things clear, Luffy still wants
to become pirate king.

00:01:58.689 --> 00:02:04.030
That part hasn’t changed, and Shanks still
gave him the straw hat, but since he is now

00:02:04.030 --> 00:02:08.450
training to be a swordsman he will also want
to someday surpass Shanks.

00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:13.810
Of course, Shanks would think this is hilarious
and will probably tell Luffy that he would

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:19.030
have to become the strongest swordsman in
the world, or something like that.

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:24.590
Which means that in addition to Luffy’s
secret dream and his desire to be Pirate King

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:28.650
[Make a list on screen], we have to add the
World’s Strongest Swordsman to his list

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:30.250
of dreams to pursue.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:34.760
However, sword training on his own can’t
last forever and eventually Luffy will probably

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:37.360
beg Shanks to take him along.

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:42.420
Of course, Shanks still won’t think he’s
ready, but he would probably agree that Luffy

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:44.920
needs someone to practice with.

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:49.890
So in our next MASSIVE CHANGE to Luffy’s
story, the Red Hair Pirates take Luffy to

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:51.590
find a master.

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:55.590
And you might be thinking Luffy is about to
go on some grand adventure, but he’s not

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:57.230
quite ready for that yet.

00:02:57.230 --> 00:03:01.120
Instead, Shanks drops Luffy off at this nearby
dojo [show Koushiro’s dojo ch 440, ch 194].

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:08.010
And is this about to get super interesting
because this is the Isshin dojo, where Zoro

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:09.940
trained during his childhood.

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:15.420
So, that’s right, Luffy and Zoro will meet
WAY EARLIER in the story.

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:20.310
And I can just imagine young Luffy and Zoro
instantly becoming fierce rivals, and if we’re

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:24.970
being honest probably good friends as well,
since both of them will be getting beat up

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:27.790
by the daughter of the dojo master, Kuina
[ch 5].

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:32.280
However, each of their desires to become the
world’s strongest swordsman or woman is

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:37.709
going to lead to a ton of intense training
and fierce duels.

00:03:37.709 --> 00:03:42.320
Now, there’s no telling really how long
this period in Luffy’s life would last,

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:47.840
but let’s just say after a year or so something
happens that is going to completely change

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:49.830
Luffy’s life.

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:54.780
Because as we know, when Shanks returned to
the Grand Line, he told people about this

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:59.190
kid in the East Blue who reminds him of the
former pirate king.

00:03:59.190 --> 00:04:05.110
Even more so now because Luffy is also using
a sword, just like Roger.

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:09.810
And this bit of news has now caught the interest
of one man in particular.

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:13.780
So one day at the dojo during another round
of Luffy and Zoro beating up on each other,

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:16.949
a small ship sails up to the Village [ch 49
shows Mihawk’s ship].

00:04:16.949 --> 00:04:22.820
And out of this ship walks a man with a large
black blade on his back, who is of course

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:29.550
none other than the current Strongest Swordsman
in the World, Dracule Mihawk.

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:31.220
Get ready for this!

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:37.310
So of course the boys will want to immediately
challenge Mihawk, but Kuina would wisely hold

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:40.600
them down while the Warlord talks to the dojo
master, Koushiro.

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:46.410
Still though, you simply can’t hold Luffy
back, so let’s say he escapes and charges

00:04:46.410 --> 00:04:48.940
Mihawk with a katana from the dojo.

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:55.860
Now this could very well be the end of Swordsman
Luffy, but let’s imagine that Mihawk whips

00:04:55.860 --> 00:05:00.030
out his tiny neck dagger and allows Luffy
to test himself.

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:06.820
But come on, there is just no way Luffy is
doing anything against this man, and eventually

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:09.940
Mihawk sends him flying across the village.

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:16.610
However, this is Luffy we’re talking about
so of course he would get up and come charging

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:18.130
right back.

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:23.290
And while Mihawk praises his determination,
he smacks Luffy again, knocking him out, and

00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:25.830
then decides he’s seen enough.

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:30.040
Before he heads back to his ship though, I
could imagine him sharing drinks with Koushiro,

00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:33.970
who has always seemed like a respectable swordsman.

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:40.229
And while the kids are obviously excluded,
that doesn’t stop them from sneaking a peek

00:05:40.229 --> 00:05:42.860
at Mihawk’s legendary sword.

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:46.400
Eventually though, time is up and Mihawk decides
to leave.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:51.910
Zoro is still itching to challenge Mihawk
himself, but Kuina keeps a firm hold on him

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:55.539
to keep him from making the same mistake as
Luffy.

00:05:55.539 --> 00:05:59.830
Whew, that could’ve been really bad, but
the kids immediately jump back into training

00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:03.110
after being energized by the surprise visit.

00:06:03.110 --> 00:06:06.030
There’s only one problem though.

00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:08.699
Luffy is nowhere to be seen.

00:06:08.699 --> 00:06:10.740
So where is he?

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:13.360
Did he get knocked into the forest and get
lost?

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:16.780
Is he crying at his failure to beat Mihawk?

00:06:16.780 --> 00:06:18.599
No, come on.

00:06:18.599 --> 00:06:20.720
This is Luffy we’re talking about.

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:27.690
Turns out that after Mihawk has sailed quite
far from the island, he turns and finds Luffy

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:33.400
being dragged along by a rope that he tied
to Mihawk’s ship, kinda similar to this

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:34.639
guy right here [show Oden dragging behind
Whitebeard’s ship ch 964].

00:06:34.639 --> 00:06:40.780
Now when Luffy climbs up onto the ship, he
expects Mihawk to be annoyed, but of course

00:06:40.780 --> 00:06:45.590
with Mihawk’s observation haki he knew Luffy
was there all along.

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:52.030
And when Mihawk asks what Luffy wants, the
young swordsman demands that Mihawk train

00:06:52.030 --> 00:06:54.770
him so that he can one day surpass him.

00:06:54.770 --> 00:06:59.150
And honestly, at this point, Mihawk would
probably throw Luffy off the ship.

00:06:59.150 --> 00:07:04.660
But let's imagine that with Luffy’s determination
plus what Mihawk already knows about him,

00:07:04.660 --> 00:07:09.370
he tells Luffy that if he can hang onto the
outside of the ship all the way through Reverse

00:07:09.370 --> 00:07:12.530
Mountain then he will train the boy.

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:20.900
Now, Luffy will obviously be super excited,
but this is a harder challenge than it seems.

00:07:20.900 --> 00:07:25.411
Remember Luffy and the crew were nearly thrown
off their ship when they went through reverse

00:07:25.411 --> 00:07:29.940
mountain, so how will he do hanging off the
side?

00:07:29.940 --> 00:07:34.430
Of course he doesn’t have his devil fruit,
so he doesn’t have to worry about losing

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:35.650
his strength in the water.

00:07:35.650 --> 00:07:41.129
But in the end after fighting off some hungry
fish, Luffy overcomes the challenge and together

00:07:41.129 --> 00:07:48.650
the World’s Strongest Swordsman and child
Luffy head off to Mihawk’s dark, spooky

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:49.650
Castle [ch 592].

00:07:49.650 --> 00:07:51.129
Now, of course Luffy is super excited.

00:07:51.129 --> 00:07:57.379
I mean what up and coming swordsman WOULDN’T
WANT to be trained by the legendary Mihawk.

00:07:57.379 --> 00:08:02.710
However, there’s some serious danger here
that we simply cannot overlook.

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:06.211
Because remember that when Zoro landed on
Mihawk’s island, the World’s Strongest

00:08:06.211 --> 00:08:12.240
Swordsman made him fight these savage sword-wielding
mandrills as the first part of his training

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:13.240
[ch 592].

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:19.569
And wow, if Zoro had trouble with these apes
then child Luffy is surely going to be in

00:08:19.569 --> 00:08:20.620
serious trouble though.

00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:25.850
So let’s imagine that Mihawk gives Luffy
some sort of training first before making

00:08:25.850 --> 00:08:28.389
him fight the island’s beasts.

00:08:28.389 --> 00:08:33.779
On top of that though, Luffy is also going
to have to learn how to take care of himself

00:08:33.779 --> 00:08:37.110
because Mihawk won’t always be at the castle.

00:08:37.110 --> 00:08:41.220
So he’d need to learn how to cook and take
care of himself.

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:44.340
So he’s leveling up in all sorts of ways.

00:08:44.340 --> 00:08:51.089
Now, let’s say that after a few years, Luffy
has improved his swordsmanship to an ABSURD

00:08:51.089 --> 00:08:56.280
degree and has even started to learn the basics
of Armament and Observation haki.

00:08:56.280 --> 00:09:04.050
Which is a stupidly massive advantage that
we’ll talk about in just a moment.

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:09.640
First though, Mihawk finally decides to take
him out to fight actual pirates, but something

00:09:09.640 --> 00:09:14.519
is going to happen next that is going to absolutely
ruin Luffy’s training.

00:09:14.519 --> 00:09:18.240
Because let’s say they run into a random
group of pirates.

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:23.209
And as Mihawk takes down the captain he tells
Luffy to wipe out the rest of the crew.

00:09:23.209 --> 00:09:31.590
And he does, quite easily after all of his
training, BUT there’s one major problem.

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:37.019
When Mihawk comes back he finds that Luffy
has taken out all the underlings, BUT he has

00:09:37.019 --> 00:09:41.230
refused to cut even a single one of them.

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:48.709
It seems Swordsman Luffy just can’t bring
himself to actually kill someone, so he basically

00:09:48.709 --> 00:09:51.930
beat them down with the dull side of the sword.

00:09:51.930 --> 00:09:58.190
Which of course would be deeply problematic
for Mihawk, who has no trouble cutting down

00:09:58.190 --> 00:09:59.200
opponents.

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:02.519
So he demands that Luffy finish the job.

00:10:02.519 --> 00:10:03.519
But…

00:10:03.519 --> 00:10:12.340
Luffy just can’t, so Mihawk finishes the
job and they return to the castle at a major

00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:14.380
crossroads.

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:16.560
Mihawk gives Luffy a choice.

00:10:16.560 --> 00:10:21.320
Decide to use his sword to its fullest and
continue his training OR leave the island

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:22.320
for good.

00:10:22.320 --> 00:10:28.010
And this is honestly kinda heartbreaking,
since Mihawk has trained Luffy more than anyone

00:10:28.010 --> 00:10:29.010
ever did.

00:10:29.010 --> 00:10:37.649
But Luffy just can’t bring himself to do
it for now, so he makes the sad choice to

00:10:37.649 --> 00:10:39.829
leave.

00:10:39.829 --> 00:10:42.410
Props to him for sticking to his gut though

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:48.720
Now, there are a few options that would make
sense for what happens next.

00:10:48.720 --> 00:10:54.040
I don’t think Mihawk would just completely
abandon Luffy, so maybe he’d give him to

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:56.860
someone he knows has a good reputation.

00:10:56.860 --> 00:11:01.560
For example, someone like Whitebeard who is
well known for taking orphans into his crew.

00:11:01.560 --> 00:11:06.200
He could also try to take him back to Shanks,
but honestly I think the most reasonable option

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:09.580
would be for Luffy to return to his hometown.

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:14.960
So back to Goa Kingdom it is.

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:19.510
And this is actually the perfect time for
Luffy to come back.

00:11:19.510 --> 00:11:24.810
Because while he doesn’t exactly have a
home here, at this point Luffy should be perfectly

00:11:24.810 --> 00:11:30.410
capable of taking care of himself in the forest
and even befriending these two ruffians [Show

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:31.410
young Sabo and Ace in the tree house ch 583].

00:11:31.410 --> 00:11:36.670
And while this is a bit later in the timeline
for the boys to meet, I’m sure they would

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:40.690
get along just like normal and quickly become
great friends.

00:11:40.690 --> 00:11:45.550
In fact, the only reason Ace and Sabo were
hesitant to take in originally was Luffy because

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:51.889
he was young and weak, but this time there
is no doubt that Luffy is even stronger than

00:11:51.889 --> 00:11:53.320
the older boys.

00:11:53.320 --> 00:11:57.810
So yeah, remember that scoreboard where Luffy
had zero wins [ch 585 has the scoreboard near

00:11:57.810 --> 00:11:58.810
the start]?

00:11:58.810 --> 00:12:01.900
I’m sure that’s going to be way different
this time around.

00:12:01.900 --> 00:12:04.470
Now let’s skip forward a bit.

00:12:04.470 --> 00:12:08.260
Sabo still decides to leave and gets blown
up [ch 588], which just leaves Ace and Luffy.

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:12.259
And here is where we get our next major change
to the story.

00:12:12.259 --> 00:12:20.110
Because when Ace leaves, there is no way Swordsman
Luffy is staying behind even though he’s

00:12:20.110 --> 00:12:22.170
only 14 years old.

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:26.720
Because even though he still wants to become
Pirate King, he is also determined to become

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:33.930
the World’s Strongest Swordsman, and he
certainly can’t do that sitting on the island.

00:12:33.930 --> 00:12:40.399
So since he is already so powerful, Swordsman
Luffy is coming along for the ride.

00:12:40.399 --> 00:12:48.920
And if you’ve read the Ace novels, you’ll
know what happens next.

00:12:48.920 --> 00:12:55.170
The short of it is they get shipwrecked, Ace
eats his devil fruit, then they journey through

00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:59.250
Sabaody, Fishman Island, and then eventually
reach Wano.

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:04.889
Then after leaving the Wano, Ace travels around
looking to take down some Yonko, but let’s

00:13:04.889 --> 00:13:05.889
back up.

00:13:05.889 --> 00:13:12.670
Because while we are in the Land of the Samurai,
Swordsman Luffy is going to hop off the train.

00:13:12.670 --> 00:13:17.959
At this point Luffy is about fifteen years
old and he is just absolutely in love with

00:13:17.959 --> 00:13:22.420
the idea of training with some actual samurai,
so even though it is hard for him to leave

00:13:22.420 --> 00:13:28.120
his friend, Swordsman Luffy cannot resist
the chance to improve his skills.

00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:34.420
The only problem is that Wano is currently
ruled by Kaido and most of the real samurai

00:13:34.420 --> 00:13:37.579
have been killed or locked up.

00:13:37.579 --> 00:13:40.560
But let’s say Luffy travels around for a
bit.

00:13:40.560 --> 00:13:45.850
Maybe he even picks up a ranked sword since
this is Wano and I’m sure they have a few

00:13:45.850 --> 00:13:47.220
of those lying around.

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:52.190
I can even see him making some friends in
the lawless lands and the Leftovers town [ch

00:13:52.190 --> 00:13:53.940
929 shows Ebisu town] outside the capitol.

00:13:53.940 --> 00:13:58.880
But this is where things are going to get
really bad.

00:13:58.880 --> 00:14:03.960
Because I for one just cannot imagine Luffy
sitting back and letting his friends in the

00:14:03.960 --> 00:14:05.790
Leftovers town starve to death.

00:14:05.790 --> 00:14:09.585
So maybe he does something rash like attack
a food shipment [ch 917 has some panels of

00:14:09.585 --> 00:14:12.180
a food shipment] or something and he steals
food for the town.

00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:16.010
Well, this is of course going to get him in
major trouble.

00:14:16.010 --> 00:14:20.890
Because we all know what happened when Luffy
did this originally [ch 921, Kaido comes down

00:14:20.890 --> 00:14:21.890
to village].

00:14:21.890 --> 00:14:24.070
Yeah, that’s not going to end well.

00:14:24.070 --> 00:14:29.540
Because as strong as Luffy is with his sword
skills, his haki - which should be pretty

00:14:29.540 --> 00:14:38.100
good after a year of traveling with Ace - he
is still only fifteen and way weaker than

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:39.760
an Emperor of the Sea.

00:14:39.760 --> 00:14:47.029
Which means he is probably getting slapped
by Kaido [end of ch 923].

00:14:47.029 --> 00:14:51.209
However, I believe this brief fight would
probably be the perfect time for Luffy to

00:14:51.209 --> 00:14:53.250
awaken his conqueror’s haki.

00:14:53.250 --> 00:14:59.459
And even though it wouldn’t do anything
against Kaido, it might impress the king of

00:14:59.459 --> 00:15:05.420
the beasts enough to throw Luffy in prison
instead of straight up killing him.

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:11.149
But you won’t believe what is going to happen
next, because who else do we know in this

00:15:11.149 --> 00:15:12.870
same prison Luffy?

00:15:12.870 --> 00:15:18.300
Well, there is of course this old man, known
as Grandpa Hyo [ch 934].

00:15:18.300 --> 00:15:19.830
And who is this man?

00:15:19.830 --> 00:15:25.649
Well, just the most famous yakuza boss in
Wano Country who also happens to know the

00:15:25.649 --> 00:15:28.759
secrets of advanced armament haki [ch 939,
Hyogoro explains basics of Ryou].

00:15:28.759 --> 00:15:36.009
So after befriending the old man and learning
his secrets, Luffy goes through his own little

00:15:36.009 --> 00:15:37.009
training arc.

00:15:37.009 --> 00:15:43.569
Now, you might think it is a bit early for
Luffy to learn advanced haki.

00:15:43.569 --> 00:15:49.459
And you might be right, but remember he has
trained with basic haki for at least five

00:15:49.459 --> 00:15:55.980
years at this point AND traveled the seas
for a year with Ace, so I’d say he has more

00:15:55.980 --> 00:16:02.040
than enough experience to learn advanced haki
at this point.

00:16:02.040 --> 00:16:10.610
So with his new skills, Luffy frees himself,
beats up the warden [Babanuki ch 934], and

00:16:10.610 --> 00:16:11.970
leads a prison break.

00:16:11.970 --> 00:16:17.450
This makes Luffy a hero for the escaped prisoners
and they gladly offer to teach Luffy their

00:16:17.450 --> 00:16:20.519
legendary swordsmanship in the outskirts of
Wano.

00:16:20.519 --> 00:16:23.100
Which is exactly what he wanted!

00:16:23.100 --> 00:16:28.000
However, Luffy’s journey in Wano is going
to end with a massive tragedy.

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:33.600
Because Kaido won’t just let a prison break
go unpunished, so I could see him sending

00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:38.370
someone like the All-Star Jack to recapture
the prisoners.

00:16:38.370 --> 00:16:45.060
And while Luffy puts up a good fight, Jack’s
thick Mammoth skin isn’t damaged at all

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:49.339
by Luffy’s dull blade attacks [ch 809],
remember he still doesn’t want to cut anyone

00:16:49.339 --> 00:16:50.339
at this point.

00:16:50.339 --> 00:16:56.339
This means that no one can defeat Jack, and
in the end, Grandpa Hyo and the other prisoners

00:16:56.339 --> 00:16:59.959
sacrifice themselves to allow Luffy to escape.

00:16:59.959 --> 00:17:05.430
Which absolutely breaks Luffy’s heart.

00:17:05.430 --> 00:17:11.380
Seriously, this would be the first major setback
in his life.

00:17:11.380 --> 00:17:16.640
But now Luffy finally understands what Mihawk
was trying to teach him as a kid.

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:21.079
Being a swordsman is about knowing when to
cut and when to not cut.

00:17:21.079 --> 00:17:27.480
And Luffy will never truly be a master if
he never chooses to cut anything.

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:33.330
So Luffy decides that he will continue his
journey and allow himself to cut down anyone

00:17:33.330 --> 00:17:35.400
who tries to hurt his friends.

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:43.000
Sadly it is a painful lesson, but one that
was important for Luffy to learn.

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:44.970
So now what?

00:17:44.970 --> 00:17:50.500
Luffy is already at the end of the Grand Line,
but he isn’t anywhere close to reaching

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:52.679
the top level of fighters in the world.

00:17:52.679 --> 00:17:58.210
So honestly, I think he chooses to finally
start his own pirate journey and conquer the

00:17:58.210 --> 00:18:00.970
Grand Line like he was always meant to do.

00:18:00.970 --> 00:18:06.880
So let’s say he steals a ship and he travels
all the way back to Reverse Mountain.

00:18:06.880 --> 00:18:12.990
This of course would take a long time, especially
on his own, so now he's seventeen years old

00:18:12.990 --> 00:18:17.650
and basically starting his journey at roughly
the same time.

00:18:17.650 --> 00:18:23.289
Now at this point, there is one major question
we simply must address.

00:18:23.289 --> 00:18:24.289
Because you might be wondering.

00:18:24.289 --> 00:18:26.600
What about the other Straw Hats?

00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:32.540
If he is skipping the East Blue then will
he ever have Zoro, Nami, Usopp, and Sanji

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:33.540
join the crew?

00:18:33.540 --> 00:18:35.760
Well, the easy answer with Zoro is no.

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:41.340
I don’t think Zoro would ever join Luffy’s
crew if he sees him as a rival for the Swords

00:18:41.340 --> 00:18:45.970
Strongest Swordsman title, but don't worry,
we’ll see more of Zoro in just a moment.

00:18:45.970 --> 00:18:50.500
The others though, well it might surprise
you that he is actually going to run into

00:18:50.500 --> 00:18:51.960
Nami very soon.

00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:57.500
Because remember her goal early on was to
steal a map of the Grand Line, so let’s

00:18:57.500 --> 00:19:02.090
assume that she also made her way to the start
of the Grand Line to steal some treasure.

00:19:02.090 --> 00:19:08.570
And let’s conveniently assume that she runs
into Luffy, and after seeing how Luffy is

00:19:08.570 --> 00:19:11.550
strong, she agrees to tag along with him.

00:19:11.550 --> 00:19:13.909
BUT there is one condition.

00:19:13.909 --> 00:19:18.860
Luffy must go back to the East Blue and defeat
Arlong to free her village.

00:19:18.860 --> 00:19:24.970
Which at this point would be no problem at
all for Swordsman Luffy.

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:30.380
Sure he doesn’t have his devil fruit, but
he already knows advanced armament and basic

00:19:30.380 --> 00:19:38.870
observation haki, so without a doubt, Luffy
could wipe out Arlong’s whole crew with

00:19:38.870 --> 00:19:40.340
ease.

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:45.230
Which means Nami is 100% ready to follow Luffy
anywhere.

00:19:45.230 --> 00:19:48.169
Now the real question is, what about the rest
of the crew?

00:19:48.169 --> 00:19:52.679
And here I’m going to make a lot of you
angry because I think at this point Luffy

00:19:52.679 --> 00:19:56.910
is much less interested in traveling around
the East Blue.

00:19:56.910 --> 00:20:03.530
He is desperate to head back to the Grand
Line and find some strong opponents to fight,

00:20:03.530 --> 00:20:06.840
which means he’s going to miss out on Usopp
and Sanji as well.

00:20:06.840 --> 00:20:10.350
I do think it would be fitting for him to
run into Zoro though.

00:20:10.350 --> 00:20:16.929
At this point, Zoro has become a famous bounty
hunter, but he is simply no match for Luffy

00:20:16.929 --> 00:20:17.929
AT ALL.

00:20:17.929 --> 00:20:22.910
Which just means that Zoro will swear to train
harder and fight Luffy again in the future.

00:20:22.910 --> 00:20:26.820
So we’re all packed up and ready to go.

00:20:26.820 --> 00:20:32.809
Luffy and Nami head off to the Grand Line,
where their first goal is to find some strong

00:20:32.809 --> 00:20:34.240
opponents to fight.

00:20:34.240 --> 00:20:40.520
And the closest big bad around is the Warlord
Crocodile who is in the process of conquering

00:20:40.520 --> 00:20:41.520
Alabasta.

00:20:41.520 --> 00:20:47.620
Now, Luffy may not have the same connection
to the Alabasta Princess, Vivi, but I’m

00:20:47.620 --> 00:20:51.070
sure he would want to fight Crocodile nonetheless.

00:20:51.070 --> 00:20:55.799
And this time around, Luffy wouldn’t even
need to figure out that sand is weak to water

00:20:55.799 --> 00:20:59.600
since Luffy already knows high levels of haki.

00:20:59.600 --> 00:21:06.059
So this fight quickly ends with Luffy slashing
the Warlord to sandy bits.

00:21:06.059 --> 00:21:12.000
Which brings us to our next MAJOR development
for Swordsman Luffy.

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:17.510
Because with Crocodile defeated we now must
ask the question, what happens to Nico Robin?

00:21:17.510 --> 00:21:24.289
Clearly, SHE would want to tag along since
Luffy has shown himself to be quite powerful,

00:21:24.289 --> 00:21:27.010
but would Luffy let her join?

00:21:27.010 --> 00:21:29.570
Honestly, I think yes.

00:21:29.570 --> 00:21:33.510
Even though at this point Luffy doesn’t
know Robin’s importance of finding the One

00:21:33.510 --> 00:21:42.230
Piece, he would still probably trust her gut
and let her join the crew.

00:21:42.230 --> 00:21:47.360
So yeah, it’s just Luffy and two women sailing
around the seas.

00:21:47.360 --> 00:21:51.130
Which, hey, Swordsman Luffy is a different
kinda guy.

00:21:51.130 --> 00:21:59.620
And now that we have two crewmates, it’s
time for a proper ship.

00:21:59.620 --> 00:22:04.320
Since Luffy has already traveled through the
Grand Line with Ace, he would probably already

00:22:04.320 --> 00:22:07.640
know about the Shipbuilding island, Water
7.

00:22:07.640 --> 00:22:11.360
So the crew heads there to buy a proper ship.

00:22:11.360 --> 00:22:17.029
One thing to keep in mind though is that on
this island there are government secret agents

00:22:17.029 --> 00:22:18.540
who are going to kidnap Robin.

00:22:18.540 --> 00:22:25.580
And we can imagine this would still occur,
but this time around things are going to turn

00:22:25.580 --> 00:22:28.510
out WAY DIFFERENTLY.

00:22:28.510 --> 00:22:33.460
Because originally when Luffy fought these
guys [show CP9 ch 347 or 349] he got absolutely

00:22:33.460 --> 00:22:37.190
crushed, but now things are a bit different.

00:22:37.190 --> 00:22:43.500
However, before anyone can swing a sword,
I believe the CP9 agents would have an invitation

00:22:43.500 --> 00:22:44.500
for Luffy.

00:22:44.500 --> 00:22:49.620
You see, since Luffy defeated Crocodile there
is an opening in the Warlords and the world

00:22:49.620 --> 00:22:54.779
government would probably see Luffy as an
ideal replacement.

00:22:54.779 --> 00:23:00.160
He just has to give up Robin and then he can
join.

00:23:00.160 --> 00:23:04.700
Which, honestly, Swordsman Luffy might consider
the offer.

00:23:04.700 --> 00:23:05.700
Just think about it.

00:23:05.700 --> 00:23:11.370
He could reunite with Mihawk, who is also
a Warlord, and fight tons of pirates without

00:23:11.370 --> 00:23:12.970
having to worry about the government.

00:23:12.970 --> 00:23:19.870
But in the end he still would reject the offer
and instead wipes out the government agents

00:23:19.870 --> 00:23:21.220
all by himself.

00:23:21.220 --> 00:23:28.659
Yes, yes, I am saying that Luffy solos all
of CP9.

00:23:28.659 --> 00:23:35.310
If you’re upset about that, get over it,
because Swordsman Luffy is on a whole different

00:23:35.310 --> 00:23:36.620
level.

00:23:36.620 --> 00:23:42.010
And so with their new ship ready to go, you
could say that Luffy also picks up a shipwright

00:23:42.010 --> 00:23:46.590
here, but honestly I kinda like the idea of
Luffy, Nami, and Robin going about it alone.

00:23:46.590 --> 00:23:51.400
I mean, Mihawk certainly sailed alone, so
Luffy might be inspired by his former mentor.

00:23:51.400 --> 00:23:56.150
So let’s skip ahead now to Sabaody, where
Swordsman Luffy would meet the Right Hand

00:23:56.150 --> 00:23:58.840
of the former Pirate King, Silvers Rayleigh.

00:23:58.840 --> 00:24:03.820
And of course Rayleigh has heard about Luffy
from Shanks, so while I don’t think we’d

00:24:03.820 --> 00:24:10.210
have the same auction house incident, eventually
Rayleigh would bust himself out and run into

00:24:10.210 --> 00:24:11.210
Luffy.

00:24:11.210 --> 00:24:15.080
Which would lead to their usual chat [ch 506-507]
where Rayleigh agrees to coat Luffy’s ship

00:24:15.080 --> 00:24:17.210
so he can go into the New World.

00:24:17.210 --> 00:24:23.070
So while we avoid the whole admiral and separation
incident this time around, there is one major

00:24:23.070 --> 00:24:26.600
obstacle before Luffy can head to the Grand
Line.

00:24:26.600 --> 00:24:35.960
That is of course the news about Ace’s execution,
which Luffy would absolutely want to stop.

00:24:35.960 --> 00:24:40.850
And I don’t think Luffy would be able to
sneak into the underwater prison, which means

00:24:40.850 --> 00:24:43.210
they are headed off to Marineford.

00:24:43.210 --> 00:24:50.279
And oh boy, is this going to be a major showcase
for Swordsman Luffy’s powers.

00:24:50.279 --> 00:24:56.140
Because remember this will be his first time
seeing his old mentor in many years [ch 560-561,

00:24:56.140 --> 00:24:57.140
Mihawk meets Luffy].

00:24:57.140 --> 00:25:01.600
On top of that he hasn’t seen Ace since
before the fiery pirate joined the Whitebeard

00:25:01.600 --> 00:25:02.600
pirates.

00:25:02.600 --> 00:25:06.620
Just sooo much has happened over the last
few years for Luffy.

00:25:06.620 --> 00:25:13.649
And of course I think we can say that Luffy
will impress Whitebeard once again.

00:25:13.649 --> 00:25:18.731
He may even clash with Mihawk, and while he
certainly isn’t on his mentor’s level

00:25:18.731 --> 00:25:24.990
yet, Luffy is going to put up quite a fight
with his advanced haki, conqueror’s haki,

00:25:24.990 --> 00:25:26.940
and extreme sword skills.

00:25:26.940 --> 00:25:31.029
In the end though, there is one fatal flaw
to Swordsman Luffy.

00:25:31.029 --> 00:25:37.220
That’s because Luffy is now more of an individual,
and while he has Nami and Robin on his crew,

00:25:37.220 --> 00:25:42.049
he is missing all of the escaped prisoners
from Impel Down who originally helped in this

00:25:42.049 --> 00:25:43.049
fight.

00:25:43.049 --> 00:25:47.010
And without them to take on some of the marines,
I just don’t think Luffy is strong enough

00:25:47.010 --> 00:25:51.340
on his own to fight through all the admirals
and reach his brother.

00:25:51.340 --> 00:26:00.760
So sorry, Ace fans, he is once again going
to perish here.

00:26:00.760 --> 00:26:05.950
That’s not the end of Swordsman’s Luffy’s
story though.

00:26:05.950 --> 00:26:10.930
Because even though he is devastated by his
longtime friend’s death, I can imagine Robin

00:26:10.930 --> 00:26:15.559
helping Luffy escape and together they get
away just in time.

00:26:15.559 --> 00:26:22.159
Which is going to send Luffy into a destructive
rage, but this time Nami and Robin are there

00:26:22.159 --> 00:26:23.159
for him.

00:26:23.159 --> 00:26:27.730
Of course, Luffy will come out of this knowing
he needs to get stronger, so it still makes

00:26:27.730 --> 00:26:33.429
a lot of sense to have a two year time skip
spent training with Rayleigh.

00:26:33.429 --> 00:26:36.210
Maybe Luffy even upgrades his weapon [show
a new sword, maybe a Guts-like sword].

00:26:36.210 --> 00:26:41.299
And since Luffy is further along with his
haki skills, they can spend their time perfecting

00:26:41.299 --> 00:26:46.270
his advanced haki and improving his sword
techniques.

00:26:46.270 --> 00:26:54.760
After the timeskip though, watch out because
this Luffy is going to be on a mission.

00:26:54.760 --> 00:27:01.760
There is ABSOLUTELY NO ONE who is going to
stop him in the early post-timeskip arcs.

00:27:01.760 --> 00:27:06.770
He’s going to sweep through this evil fishman
[Hoady], this corrupt scientist [Caesar],

00:27:06.770 --> 00:27:09.220
and even the stringy Warlord [Doflamingo].

00:27:09.220 --> 00:27:13.230
Although I do think he would be challenged
by his longtime rival Zoro along the way,

00:27:13.230 --> 00:27:18.840
who surprisingly has made up his own crew
including Usopp, Sanji, Chopper, and Franky.

00:27:18.840 --> 00:27:24.260
However, after learning about the Road Poneglyphs
on Zoa, Luffy can focus solely on collecting

00:27:24.260 --> 00:27:28.830
the Road Poneglyphs and finding the One Piece
because he doesn’t need to rescue Sanji

00:27:28.830 --> 00:27:32.059
from Big Mom.

00:27:32.059 --> 00:27:38.080
Which is going to take him straight to Wano
to confront one of the only people to ever

00:27:38.080 --> 00:27:39.880
defeat him, the Emperor Kaido.

00:27:39.880 --> 00:27:44.990
And I’m sure Luffy would want to go straight
up and challenge the king of the beasts.

00:27:44.990 --> 00:27:48.850
And honestly, that might not be the worst
idea.

00:27:48.850 --> 00:27:57.559
Because remember Luffy is now a truly OP swordsman
and we know Kaido has some PTSD about legendary

00:27:57.559 --> 00:28:01.350
swordsmen, so there is a very good chance
he could take down Kaido.

00:28:01.350 --> 00:28:06.750
On the other hand though, Luffy’s overconfidence
could see him get smacked down by the strongest

00:28:06.750 --> 00:28:11.820
creature in the world because remember that
Luffy could only truly damage Kaido once he

00:28:11.820 --> 00:28:14.320
unlocked his next major powerup.

00:28:14.320 --> 00:28:18.730
So let's say that Luffy gets himself in a
desperate situation.

00:28:18.730 --> 00:28:23.919
He is doing damage to Kaido, but he can’t
finish him off.

00:28:23.919 --> 00:28:29.039
But then Kaido takes it to the next level
and is about to crush Luffy with his massive

00:28:29.039 --> 00:28:30.039
club [end of ch 1042, luffy gets crushed].

00:28:30.039 --> 00:28:36.890
And with no strong crewmates to save him,
Luffy is in real trouble… until a certain

00:28:36.890 --> 00:28:41.260
green-haired swordsman swoops in and blocks
Kaido’s attack.

00:28:41.260 --> 00:28:47.940
You see, Zoro can’t stand seeing his rival
taken down by someone else, so he battles

00:28:47.940 --> 00:28:50.730
Kaido, which gives Luffy some time to recover.

00:28:50.730 --> 00:28:56.320
And during this time he also figures out the
secrets of advanced conqueror’s haki [ch

00:28:56.320 --> 00:28:57.320
1010].

00:28:57.320 --> 00:29:02.840
Then together, Luffy and Zoro fulfill Wano’s
dream of finally freeing the country from

00:29:02.840 --> 00:29:04.929
the legendary dragon.

00:29:04.929 --> 00:29:10.460
Which means Luffy has earned his second Road
Poneglyph and is truly on the path to becoming

00:29:10.460 --> 00:29:13.410
pirate king AND the World’s Strongest Swordsman.

00:29:13.410 --> 00:29:18.799
However, there are still many challenges ahead,
including confronting his two old mentors,

00:29:18.799 --> 00:29:20.470
Mihawk and Shanks.

00:29:20.470 --> 00:29:27.039
And you can bet that those two have some of
the strongest haki in the entire series, so

00:29:27.039 --> 00:29:32.370
Luffy is going to need a major powerup in
that department before he can even dream of

00:29:32.370 --> 00:29:33.730
taking them down.

00:29:33.730 --> 00:29:38.830
In fact, we’ve seen how strong Luffy has
become with Swords and Haki, but I’ve always

00:29:38.830 --> 00:29:43.690
wondered how strong Luffy would be if he ONLY
USED HAKI.

00:29:43.690 --> 00:29:44.890
No devil fruit.

00:29:44.890 --> 00:29:45.890
No swords.

00:29:45.890 --> 00:29:52.779
So if you want to see if Haki-Only Luffy is
truly the strongest, you can watch that video

00:29:52.779 --> 00:29:53.779
right here [Show Luffy Haki only].

00:29:53.779 --> 00:29:56.770
Shanks for watching and I’ll see you in
the next one.

